    <DataNode elementId="CPD-7063" textLabel="red chlorophyll catabolite" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="GVTPYCXGTFQZDT-YSSUGPPCSA-M" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="200" centerY="540" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="xue, PMN, nilo-poyanco">Common chlorophyll pathways lead to the production of a colourless, blue-fluorescing intermediate (|FRAME: CPD-7064| or pFCC) &lt;i&gt;via&lt;/i&gt; the formation of a red chlorophyll catabolite (RCC). The final steps of chlorophyll catabolism are species-specific and involve a diversity of modifications of pFCC before the catabolites are finally stored in the vacuole in the form of |FRAME:NCCS|, or NCCs |CITS:[15012204],[16448336]|.</Comment>
